3 1\nActinomycin V / A / B / D / S\n5 5 5 3 \n2.10.2 Struktureller Aufbau \nActinomycine sind Chromopeptide. Sie besitzen als gemeinsamen Actinoyl-Chromophor ein \n2-Aminophenoxazin-3-on-System, das zweifach methyliert und über zwei Amidbindungen \nmit Pentapeptidlacton-Ringen verknüpft ist. \nAls Grundstruktur kann Actinomycin D (19) angesehen werden (Abbildung 22), von dem sich \ndurch Abwandlung oder Modifikation einzelner Aminosäuren die anderen Strukturen ableiten--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ncommunications chemistry (https://pub.uni-bielefeld.de/download/3003025/3003034/s42004-025-01534-x.pdf)\nciteturn39search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; purify and characterize these yet-unknown compounds. ... Clade C (Fig. 1) contained three BGCs respectively from the azureomycin ... Of note, the structure of\nazureomycin is still unresolved. ... was found in the genome of Kutzneria sp. ... encoding for Type I balhimycin (bal) and chloroeremomycin BGC (cem).\nhttps://doi.org/10.1038/s42004-025-01534-x\nArticle\npurify and characterize these yet-unknown compounds. In this paper, we\nfocused on A. auranticolor YU 961-1 (=DSM 44650), as our preliminary\nstudies demonstrated that this strain produced the putative GPA at high\nlevel in standard cultivation conditions (see below). GPA production in U.\nendophytica DSM 103496 will be instead investigated in future.\ngeneticorganization(SupplementaryFig.3)thatcodeforthebiosynthesisof\nteicoplanin-like acylated GPAs: the product from one of them (known as\nGP1416) was previously identiﬁed from Amycolatopsis sp. WAC 0141640.\nClade C (Fig. 1) contained three BGCs respectively from the azureomycin\nproducer Amycolatopsis azurea DSM 4385461 and from two other Amyco-\nlatopsis spp. still not known to produce GPAs. Of note, the structure of\nazureomycin is still unresolved. These BGCs seemed identical in terms of\ngenetic organization (Supplementary Fig. 3). Their predicted